# BeanNote project constraints

You are working on BeanNote, a FastAPI + Tailwind PWA coffee journal. Keep changes modular and concise.

## Architecture
- `db.py`: SQLite schema, dual-env paths, users/auth, UNIQUE(name, roaster) ON CONFLICT IGNORE, fuzzy dedupe via `difflib.get_close_matches` (cutoff 0.80), queries, export.
- `ocr.py`: Gemini 1.5 Flash Vision with Tesseract fallback. Detect `/opt/homebrew/bin/tesseract` or `/usr/local/bin/tesseract`. Auto EXIF rotation via `PIL.ImageOps.exif_transpose`.
- `translations.py`: DA / EN / DE / FR / ES keys only. No inline UI copy in other files.
- Mobile header support pill uses i18n key `support_header` (DA: "☕ Støt").
- `main.py`: FastAPI API, JWT/OAuth, static PWA. No business logic that belongs in db.py/ocr.py.
- `static/index.html`: Tailwind PWA. Do not add extra frameworks or a second database.

## Environment
- `ENVIRONMENT=local` → `./data/beannote.db` (absolute wipe of beans/ratings/users on startup, no demo seed).
- `ENVIRONMENT=production` → `/app/data/beannote.db` (never auto-flush).
- `RESET_DB_ON_START=true` flushes only when not production.
- Unraid: PUID=99, PGID=100, TZ=Europe/Copenhagen, volume `/mnt/user/appdata/beannote/data`.

## Deduplication
- Always fuzzy-check before insert (manual or OCR).
- UI warning must stay: "Minder denne bønne om en eksisterende i BeanNote?" (via i18n key `duplicate_warning`) plus a 1-click jump to rate the existing bean.

## Snapshots
- After any feature or refactor, append `CHANGELOG.md` and create a git snapshot:
  `git commit -m "snapshot: vX.Y.Z - <feature>"`
- Bump VERSION in `db.py` when the change is user-facing.

## Scope
- Mobile-first PWA. Do not redesign the palette (Espresso `#3c2a21`, Terracotta `#b85c38`, Cream `#faf6f0`).
- No README expansion, no extra markdown, no drive-by refactors.
